## Context
`scripts/forge.py` is the harness's forge adapter (`--forge auto|gh|none`;
verbs resolve, comments, checks, review_state, comment, append_body_line,
create, ready, auto_merge_armed, disarm, merge, read_back, merged_at; typed
refusal and NOOP; offline cache). Its `none` backend keeps review and gate state
in git notes (`review_notes.py`, `merge-gate.py`). Raw `gh` calls that bypass it
make those steps GitHub-only: on a no-forge repository or another forge they fail
or, worse, read as "nothing found". This is the forge twin of the runtime tracker
1309. The author asked for it on 2026-10-28, in the session that mapped the
three adapter axes (runtime, forge, model door; `adapters/README.md` § Adapter map).

Raw `gh` sites on main, 2026-10-28 (`git grep -E "gh (pr|api|issue|run|repo)"`
plus the inventory of tracker 1309):
- **Landing path (highest stakes):** the merge skill's recipe prose
  (skills/merge/SKILL.md, references/claims.md); `skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh`
  (≈341, 359); `skills/roar/check-close-claims.sh`;
  `scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` (≈97-129); `scripts/review-anchor.py`.
- **Status and reports:** `skills/dashboard/dashboard.sh` (≈26-29),
  `scripts/raid-sitrep.py` (≈42), `scripts/slow_tickets.py` (≈80), `skills/lair/SKILL.md`,
  `skills/roar/runbooks/capture.md` (the extension-point hint for the PR body read).
- **Trace analytics:** `scripts/trace-pr-join.py`, `scripts/trace_merge_path.py`.
  They join Claude traces to GitHub PRs as measurement, so a GitHub dependency
  may be acceptable there; decide per site.
- **Probably legitimate:** `scripts/local-ci.sh` passes a forge token to `act`
  (a GitHub Actions runner by design).

