- trace analytics and local-ci: decide keep-with-reason or port

## Exit criteria
- [x] Every site above is routed through `forge.py` or listed as residue with its reason
- [x] Each ported site has a `none`-backend test (no `gh` on PATH) that shows the
      step still works or answers a typed NOOP, never an empty all-clear
- [x] `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` (or a forge equivalent, only if a leak recurs after
      the sweep) keeps the count from growing
- [x] `make check` passes

## Integration review (raid f7fa41, 2026-10-28, main 21e9bb9a)
Children: 1318 PR #1912, 1319 PR #1916, 1320 PR #1915, 1321 PR #1911, all merged at their
ruled heads. forge.py CLI: `list`, `files`, `read-back`; exit 0 rows, 2 could not look (origin,
no gh or gh failed), 3 no forge (no origin remote); `resolve` refuses with 1.
Residue, each with its reason at the call site or in the child's log:
- 1321 keep: trace-pr-join.py, trace_merge_path.py (regex, not a call), review_evidence.py
  (host-pinned GraphQL, fails closed), local-ci.sh (act is a GitHub Actions runner).
- 1319 keep: slow_tickets.py (needs createdAt, comments, checks; no verb; degrades to unknown).
- 1320 markers: merge/SKILL.md comment, ready, disarm, merge; claims.md body edit;
  lair/SKILL.md auto-merge setting. forge.py has these writes in Python (raid_land.py uses
  them) but no CLI; the prose keeps the gh spelling behind extension-point markers.
- Not calls: census/exec-vs-mention.py, trace-wall-time.py (pattern lists); rules/git.md example.
Union sweep (`git grep` for raw gh calls in scripts/ and skills/): only the residue above.
`env -u TMPDIR make check` on 21e9bb9a: 3009 passed, 4 skipped; check-agnostic passes;
`forge.py list` with no gh on PATH in this origin repo exits 2, dashboard says NOT inspected.
Criterion 3: check-agnostic's SKILL_PATTERNS already gate `gh ` in skills/ outside markers; no
new script-side guard, since the criterion asks for one only if a leak recurs.
